usize_ptr	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: vspec::atom::kani_atom::usize_ptr_names_its_atomic; not checked: that `r` carries `a`'s provenance, so loads and stores through it reach `a` (the harness compares addresses))	contract 1082442458, body 2711750530
# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): the class table's watermark
# (`committed_slabs`) is written only by `store_usize` and its class-line
# copy (`ClassLine::committed`) only by `store_usize_at`; only
# class/table.rs calls these wrappers and only heap/shared.rs makes a
# copy's pointer (`usize_ptr`); this file mints one UsizePerm per atomic,
# in `new_usize` (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). C++20's coherence rules
# ([intro.races]) give a load a write no older than the last one that
# happens before it, so the permission's value at its place in the
# atomic's modification order; the stores are made under the commit lock,
# which orders them, and `WatermarkPred` bounds one atomic by constants,
# so any ordering keeps it. `load_usize_seen`'s witness, the owner words
# of every group below the value read, needs the `Release` store and its
# `Acquire` load (a release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2), which the
# watermark and free models check; `load_u16_at` reads an owner word whose
# only write is `table::store_owner`'s, so a load ordered after it reads
# its value (a free not ordered after its allocation can read 0, the free
# models' documented fast-path miss). The models run copies of the
# `SlabTable` steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The GenMC watermark and
# bitmap cases run these wrappers as they are over `core`'s atomics,
# inside pinned copies of the same steps (tests/genmc/watermark.rs and
# bitmap.rs, `GENMC_PINS`), with the permissions erased (and
# `load_usize_seen`'s invariant); no case runs the free path's steps
# (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC").
store_usize	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::atom_store_usize, and loom: watermark::loom_watermark_take_group_publishes, free::loom_free_after_synchronised_handoff and bitmap::loom_bitmap_init_is_published, and GenMC: wm [rc11 imm], wm3 [rc11 imm arm8] and bitmap_init_published [rc11 imm]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the table steps, in the configurations their files state, and beyond the configurations tests/genmc/watermark.rs and bitmap.rs state, which the GenMC cases run it in as it is over `core`'s atomic inside copies of the same steps, each only under the memory models its citation names (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": no race report under ARMv8, and the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); the free path's steps, which no case runs; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the watermark's last write, which no GenMC case checks (the cases erase the permissions, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so none sees a ghost value) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3684131722, body 3052065581
